cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. The accompanying article is in preparation; its reference will be added here when a public version exists."
type: software
title: "READ-EarEOG-Repro: experimental code for detecting and evaluating return-sweep-like saccades from ear electrodes during reading"
authors:
  - given-names: Ali
    family-names: Amini
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AliAmini93/READ-EarEOG-Repro"
abstract: >-
  Python code for the experimental procedures of an exploratory study of ear-electrode
  electro-oculography during continuous-text reading: ear derivations, filtering and scaling,
  eye-tracker labels and line classes, a step-statistic detector, leave-one-recording-out
  thresholds, one-to-one event scoring, chance-level and velocity-threshold baselines,
  saccade-locked gains and d-prime, false-alarm analyses, cohort statistics and a causal
  variant. No recordings, results or figures are included.
keywords:
  - electrooculography
  - ear-eeg
  - eye-tracking
  - event-detection
  - reproducible-research
